  "content": {
    "id": "p68-q14-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The sum of two positive numbers is $30$. Find the numbers when the product is a maximum.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$15$ and $15$ (maximum product $225$).",
      "worked": "Let the numbers be $x$ and $30-x$, where $0<x<30$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=x(30-x)\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe quadratic is concave down and has zeros $0$ and $30$. Its maximum occurs halfway between the zeros, at $x=15$.\n\nThe numbers are $15$ and $15$, with maximum product $225$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
